<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: CRH says H1 pre-tax profit up 13 percent.</title>
<headline>CRH says H1 pre-tax profit up 13 percent.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		13.95		  vs 12.84</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.08		   vs 2.75</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    64.12		  vs 56.85</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,004.12	     vs 887.73</p>
<p> Trading profit	   68.94		  vs 63.05</p>
<p> Interest payable	 9.34		   vs 4.66</p>
<p> Tax charge		 13.80		  vs 11.40</p>
<p> Net taxed		  50.32		  vs 45.45</p>
<p> Registration date	September 24</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 8</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish-based building materials group CRH said it was buying BTR's U.S. unit Tilcon for $220 million and assuming Tilcon's net debt of $106 million, for a total consideration of $329 million.</p>
<p>CRH also said it was placing 17.94 million shares to raise a net 101 million punts.</p>
<p>Analysts'forecasts for CRH pre-tax profits ranged from around 62 to 66 million Irish pounds.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
